    "body": "> The bug is long but my main takeaway was that WebKit implemented this ahead of a spec ([still seems to be there](https://github.com/WebKit/webkit/blob/ae1c6da14bb6bf86cd92d9bfb3d5670043b3c00e/Source/WebCore/html/track/TextTrack.cpp#L146)). Chrome [considered it but did not](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=271185).\r\n> \r\n> Is this use case still valid? Would the WebKit team like to request that this be part of the spec and that other browsers implement? What is our path toward interop here?\r\n> \r\nYes, the use case is still valid and I think we should add `kind=forced` to the spec.\r\n\r\nThanks for digging up the old bug and filing the issue!",
