    "created_at": "2019-04-01T09:00:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-01T09:00:17Z",
    "body": "> Yes, the use case is still valid and I think we should add kind=forced to the spec.\r\n\r\nThe use case for signalling forced content is indeed relevant but it is orthogonal to the `kind` attribute. Forced could itself be a new attribute, taking values such as:\r\n\r\n* `false`: the track should not be forced to an enabled state\r\n* `true`: the track must be forced to an enabled state if `srclang` matches the user's language preference.\r\n\r\nSee also https://www.w3.org/TR/ttml-imsc1.1/#itts-forcedDisplay which allows the timed text to indicate within the content which parts need to be forced and which do not. This adds a requirement for a flag to be set when presenting to indicate if _all_ content should presented or if only the forced content should be presented.\r\n\r\nI'd propose that the Text Track `@mode` value space should be augmented from the current `Disabled|Hidden|Showing` to add a new value `ShowingForcedOnly`, to fulfil this flag requirement.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
