    "body": "@nigelmegitt it helps to read the original issue at https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=23507 to understand the full need of this feature.\r\n\r\nA \"forced\" subtitle track is like a fall-back track that is turned on when no other subtitle track is turned on - and only the \"forced\" subtitle track for your language will be turned on. So, there can be several \"forced\" subtitle track, each with a different \"language\" - and since it's not relevant when a subtitle track is selected, using \"kind\" is perfectly fine.\r\n\r\nSeparating parts of a subtitle track as \"forced\" is much harder to transcribe and isn't the way of current authoring practice.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
