    "body": "> A \"forced\" subtitle track is like a ...\r\n\r\n@silviapfeiffer the concept of \"forced\" also applies not only to subtitle tracks but also to captions and descriptions, hence it is orthogonal to `@kind`.\r\n\r\nSeparating parts of a subtitle track as \"forced\" is in fact existing practice. It simplifies asset distribution and allows authors to ensure that, if there is temporal overlap between forced and non-forced timed text, the positioning of the forced content and non-forced content is correctly defined.\r\n\r\nOf course if this means that translation and same-language timed text is in the same file that does mean that `kind` cannot usefully express the content.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
